mantle rm265
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_finn_saltwell
title the pull of a thumb
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor drive=ambitious
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk trials_fancy_knots_on_a_loaf_sling
likes warm_bread knots quiet_chapel first_snow
dislikes haggling bad_manners
fears a_loop_that_jams_under_a_load
hopes a_knot_that_slips_off_neatly
topics pastimes +0.6 work +0.5 food +0.3 prices -0.2
styles comfort=loosen gossip=plain refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# ties elaborate bread slings and looks for the one little pull that will release each knot when a load is down.

words
oath! = Nine nipped thumbs | Hoops and hemp
saying! = Leave a tail for the hungry | Pretty loops can do heavy work
sling = a soft cord sling | my loaf carrier
loop = the broad loop | a flattened eye
tail = the loose end | my thumb-long tail
crust = that russet crust | the upper crust
tag = a dry wax tag | a little waxed scrap
grip = a two-finger grip | a steady hold
coil = a whole coil | the remaining turns
loaf = a brown round loaf | a warm bread crown
snowcap = a white rim | a fresh cap of snow
mat = a braided pad | the landing mat
spare = a short cord end | the spare string
inkmark = my thumbprint | a faint dark smudge

any
opinion houses against 1 : A House gets the credit for a full hold. The backs that emptied it deserve a mention.
opinion merchants against 1 : Name the sum for the good part. I'm tired of buying weight that gets swept off the floor.
opinion sump for 1 : A bit of clean rope can live seven lives down our way. Nobody looks down on the sixth.
opinion watch against 1 : Boots arriving after a load falls aren't much help keeping your feet clear.
opinion dole for 1 : An empty bread sling means an easy climb and a bad dinner. I'm for filling it.
opinion strangers for 1 : I'd give a stranger one end of a cord. You learn quite a bit about a wolf that way.

grown
line greet : My cord's all paid out. Hello to you. | Here's a word while I take another turn.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : An unfamiliar face alongside my loose end, I see. | Welcome alongside this little operation.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Fresh light for an intricate job. Morning to you. | A decent hour to start something ambitious.
line greet.return : Yes, hello. The knot can wait while I talk. | I heard your hail over my own voice.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Good to hear that particular voice carry. | For you I'd set down a whole armload.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : Evening to you across this snarl of string. | Night's a good time for talk and a poor time for fine knots.
line again.open : We're back at the same bight of cord. | There's a bit still to be unpicked between us.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Come feel how clean this one runs! | Have a look at my latest little triumph.
line farewell : Leave plenty of slack for your journey. | A whole foot of spare cord go with you.
line farewell.return : I'll draw my end in now. Goodbye. | Off you go with a free swinging stride.
line react.news : Straight from your mouth to my ears. I'm listening. | Set the news down where I can consider the size of it.
line react.news.new : Even its loose ends had passed me by. | That's new enough to stop my thumb.
line react.news.known : Yes. I've had that bundle put to me once already. | Heard that exact turn earlier on.
line react.news.doubt : I'd give the middle of that yarn a firm tug. | I don't believe every turn in that account is sound.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : Hard hearing. I'll put this tangle down and stay. | That's the sort of weight two ought to carry together.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : Now there's a piece I'd cheer from the farthest pier. | Good hearing, up and down the whole length of me.
line ask.how : Has the day left any slack in your shoulders? | How freely have things been running?
line answer.how : Full of plans and a touch short of cord. | Quite able to pull my share and an inch more.
line decline : I'd have little chance of getting that back to you sound. | There's more in my paws than I can lay down just now.
line accept_decline : Clear enough. I'll draw the offer in. | Very well. No loose obligation between us.
line preclose : I've said enough to fill a good sized hold. | There's another piece I'm keen to try before I rest.
line accept_preclose : You've hauled your end in handsomely. Go on. | We can leave this coil just as it lies.
line thank : That spared my thumb a blister. Much obliged. | I felt your share of the pull and appreciated it.
line deflect_thanks : I'd found the good end already. The rest took little effort. | Those loops would have gone to waste otherwise.
line sympathise : You can put an untidy problem down beside me. | Some things bind tighter the longer you pull. Rest here.
line reassure : We'll slacken one turn and see what gives. | It looks a worse tangle from underneath.
line ack : I can follow that strand clean through. | That's clear along its whole length.
line give.advice : Leave yourself one end longer than you think necessary. | Practise opening the knot as well as making it.

scene loaf_trial
when topic=pastimes self.likes=knots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : This sling will carry a loaf without cutting the crust. | I'm inventing string handles for supper.
b : Why bother with string for a single loaf? | What stops the cord slicing in?
a : Wide loops. And it leaves a paw free to open doors. | I've plaited three soft ends flat where they touch the crust.

scene earn_pull
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An elegant lift isn't much use if the landing takes all morning. | I like a load to come out of its cords clean.
b : Does the last knot take longest? | What keeps a landing slow?
a : Usually somebody tied it for sailing all the way round the world. | A tight turn where the slack tail ought to be. Very small nuisance, very large delay.

scene tailbit
when topic=work self.job=sailor self.working=yes
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Leave that little tail showing. | Give the free end a bit of daylight.
b : Looks untidy to me. | Does daylight make cord stronger?
a : So does a long delay while we pick the whole knot out. | No, but somebody can see which end wants pulling.

scene warmcargo
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can tell how fresh the loaf is without cutting it. | Warm cargo makes a particular announcement.
b : Does your nose do the work? | What does your sling tell you?
a : My wrist. It warms up through the cord before the smell reaches me. | If the crust warms my wrist, I've got a good hot middle for dinner.

scene snowdeck
when topic=weather here.weather=snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New snow will show you which end of a cord moved last. | One twitch leaves a neat little drawing in this snow.
b : Is that why you're looking down? | What drawing does a cord make?
a : Yes. That line between the marks was made by the tail sliding. | Two little bumps with a track between. Quite a tidy signature.

scene quiet_seat
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : A quiet chapel is the one place I'm glad not to hear my own voice. | Even I can put a lid on the talk for a quiet chapel.
b : Your voice does carry. | Do the ropes get a rest too?
a : I know. Sometimes I take a back seat and let the silence carry instead. | I keep my cord safely pocketed. Prayers needn't have knots in them.

scene no_bargain
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I'd pay a fair asking sum quickly and go straight to work. | A long bargain can eat the saving in lost time.
b : Even if you could do better? | You put a price on talking?
a : Especially then. I could spend all day beating it lower and never eat. | On standing about repeating a number, certainly.

scene seal
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd carry a folded letter inside a wrap of waxed cloth. | A letter at sea ought to travel drier than the messenger.
b : Have you tried it? | How would you wrap it?
a : I've carried one about long enough to test my method in ordinary rain. | Fold the cloth down over the writing. Let the drops fall clear of the fold.

scene share_code
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a little trick with this sling I'd show #self.friend# first. | I'd save a choice scrap of cord for #self.friend#.
b : What makes it choice? | Would you keep it secret?
a : Soft enough for practising a new loop without fraying the pads. | Only till somebody dear to me has first go. Then I'd tell a whole pier.

scene poor_end
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When coin runs thin I start inspecting every frayed end again. | A worn bit of stuff's worth unlaying if times pinch.
b : Can any of it do a job? | What would you make from that?
a : Plenty. A short scrap can secure a cover as well as anything fine. | A new cord plaited from the middle strands. Those keep their strength longest.

scene knee_mat
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the Sump I could do with a woven mat for a load on damp boards. | I've plans for a little raised pad outside my own door.
b : What for? | Why raised?
a : To keep the underside of a bundle out of standing water. | A half inch saves you wringing half your gear out again.

scene gate_hours
when topic=day here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gate gives a town two pulses, out in the morning and in before dark. | Count the laden carts through Northgate and you'll see the day turn.
b : You count the carts? | Which movements interest you?
a : Only when I'm held up myself. Gives a delay some occupation. | The change from laden going out to laden coming in. Different sound to the wheels, too.

scene wet_knot
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Let a wet knot rest before you get cross with it. | Tugging at that wet cord won't teach it obedience.
b : Am I meant to wait all afternoon? | Looks as if it's stuck.
a : Ease it sideways. Gives the fat wet fibres a bit of room. | Press the turns apart with the heel of your paw first. See, that one's moving.

scene silence
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I can shift news fast when it's news of my own business. | Another wolf's letter needs no extra words on the outside.
b : Sure you haven't peeked? | You do like words, though.
a : I like a clean reputation more than half a story. | Oh, a warehouse full. Just ones I've a right to use.

scene bread_dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My aim's a sling that opens at a brush of my thumb. | Some day I'll have supper out while everybody else is still untying the strings.
b : Anything else going in this invention? | You'd put that much work into a bread bag?
a : Nothing heavier than the loaf. It wants a clever shape, not more iron. | Gladly. I'd save enough time to eat my dinner warm.

scene rude_arms
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=bad_manners
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I could forgive an interruption sooner than an elbow put across my load. | I'd like folk to leave swinging space for a laden wolf to turn.
b : The load gets manners too? | That happened before?
a : The load has none. That's why the wolf beside it needs a few. | Often enough to put a decent swing on my elbow if I weren't careful.

scene festival_coil
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A braid round a festival basket makes even ordinary bread look grand. | I like a busy festival basket to have a knot you can open one-handed.
b : You've ambitious plans for a knot. | Do you eat the braid too?
a : Give me enough decent cord and I'll show you. | The braid just gets you into the bread before the good pieces go.

scene tall_call
when topic=ships self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My voice carries well, but you won't hear me shouting across a loaded sling. | Best call you can make in a noisy yard sometimes fits into two notes.
b : Would anyone hear a quiet call? | What do the two notes mean?
a : A call pitched high and then low cuts clean across a rumble. | Look this way. After that you can see my paw.

grown

story split_loaf [topic=memories|food]
  : Made a fancy sling once with a double turn just where my supper lay.
  : Brought home my loaf neatly halved and one smug-looking knot.
  b : Was the sling any use after that?
  : For parcelled things, yes. For supper I've given the cord new orders.

story snow_letter [topic=travel|memories]
  : On a snowy errand I had a message to carry and wrapped the writing in so much cloth it looked like a meal.
  : Got hungry enough to open my own parcel by mistake.
  b : Was the paper at least dry?
  : Dry as flour. It made me all the hungrier to see it.

story thumbprint [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I used to make a little dark mark on the end that opened a difficult knot.
  : Rubbed my nose after marking three of them. Spent an afternoon going round with three black spots.
  b : Did anybody mention the spots?
  : No. That's what gets me. I lost an afternoon of good-natured boasting.

rule @tail
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A thumb's breadth extra at the loose end! | I'd rather see an extra tail than an extra tangle.

rule @lift
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=sailor
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hold till there's room for the sling to land! | All clear below and I'll lower it.

rule @crust
when concept=bark self.likes=warm_bread
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Mind that lovely thin crust under the cord. | A hot loaf's worth taking a clean sling for.

rule @flakes
when concept=bark here.weather=snow
does aside
cooldown 8h
say You can see every turn in the white now. | Fresh snow and a good black cord make a legible diagram.

dlg resident.hub : I'll give you a straight account provided you've time for both ends and the middle.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, see how neatly this bit of trouble comes apart now.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=dawn] : Good light and a clear length of day ahead. I'd call that a promising start.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'll give you an answer with my belongings on this side of me.
dlg resident.job [self.job=sailor] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I always have an eye on what it'll take to get a load unwrapped.
dlg resident.job : A complicated beginning and a clean finish suit me in any work.
dlg resident.bye : There's a generous piece of daylight left for your own use.

graft resident.hub
choice Which end frees your bread sling? -> breadtail
node breadtail
say The little end folded back on itself. Catch it against your thumb first and slip the whole thing off. Doesn't take near so long as explaining it.
free
choice What if I pull the other one? -> shutloop
choice That ought to save the crust. -> hub
node shutloop
say Then I get the interesting part. There's supper in there and an ambitious appetite makes a good knot-picker.
choice I'll leave you the cord. -> hub
choice Good luck with supper. -> bye
